# Gumbo, the elephant from "Advanced RenderMan" (Apodaca and Gritz): 128 bicubic Bezier
# patches (models/gumbo.rib in models/patches.zip), each evaluated on a 10 x 10 lattice and
# written as triangles by tools/gumbo_from_rib.py, with the exact patch normal at every vertex.
# LEFT-HANDED, RenderMan convention: x right, y up, +z into the screen. 1 unit tall.
# Stands on y = 0, centered at x = 0 and z = 0, faces -z (toward a camera looking down +z).
# Viewers that assume a right-handed OBJ (Blender, MeshLab) will show it mirrored. That is expected.
# Every face corner uses one index for v, vt, and vn (already unwelded); the texture
# coordinates are each patch's own (u, v), with t = 0 at the BOTTOM row (OBJ convention).
mtllib gumbo.mtl

